doc('MATH_REVIEW.md',r'''# Full03 mathematical review

The literal nonexistence theorem is verified relative to the explicitly named published topology inputs. No mathematical gap was identified in that deduction. This does not reprove the topology papers, certify novelty, or decide Casson-zero cases.

My INITIAL_ATTACK predates all assessment intake. For any finite set of sizes choose a rank coordinate containing them, represented by a finite polynomial P(t). In D=Z[x]/x², q=1+x and q⁻¹=1−x. The coefficient completion maps to D through its second coordinate. For P(t)=sum(a_j+b_j x)t^j, evaluation at q^n has constant sum a_j and first coefficient sum b_j+n sum j a_j. This is affine for every chosen finite set. Evaluation before taking the jet is legitimate at a containing rank coordinate because its defining polynomial vanishes exactly. The written candidate's quadratic third-coordinate proof is the same valid consequence in a minimal sufficient coordinate. It divides by a monic polynomial, never by a node difference or nilpotent. Neither Taylor injectivity nor an inverse-limit/tensor exchange is needed.

The source ring really inverts only q. At finite coefficient level, the defining polynomial has unit constant term, which explicitly makes q a unit already; this identification commutes with the quotient maps. The displayed sl_n uses matrix size n and assigns I_1=1. These facts were checked visually in the exact primary printed490–492. The assignment's zero-based page labels were offset from the locally rendered printed labels; I inspected actual one-based PDF118–120 (printed490–492), and also extracted the assigned119–121 range. This bookkeeping discrepancy changed no mathematical intake or conclusion.

Published inputs were independently retrieved and read: Lê2000, p815 fixes Cartan root lengths and q=1+x; pp818–820 construct the projective perturbative series; p821 states the coefficient c1=|H1|^{-n(n−1)/2} n(n²−1)lambda_C, in the prose after the separate integrality conjecture. Habiro–Lê2016 Theorem1.1/Propositions1.2 and1.9 identify the unified, projective and Taylor targets. Section3A1–2 uses short roots squared length2 and q=v²=exp(h), uniformly in typeA. These are source-level theorem inputs, not conclusions of the finite programs. The cardinality of trivial H1 is1. No Legendre factor or rank-dependent parameter remains on integral spheres.

For the orientation given by minus-one surgery on a left-hand trefoil, the primary Poincare series has polynomial summand q^k(1+...+q^k) product_{j=k+2}^{2k+1}(1−q^j). The constant term is1, the k=1 first coefficient is−6, and every k≥2 summand lies in x^k. Habiro v1 equation16.1 explicitly gives the same series as a unified invariant. Thus the whole tail, not a finite sample of it, vanishes in the first jet. One may also express its k-th summand as q^k[k+1]_q [2k+1 choose k]_q product_{j=1}^k(1−q^j); the Gaussian polynomial identity proves Habiro-ideal convergence. Calibration in the cited coefficient formula fixes lambda_C=−1 and gives sizes1,2,3 slopes0,−6,−24. Their second difference is−12 instead of0. For arbitrary nonzero integer lambda_C the residual is12lambda_C. The sizes2,3,4 residual18lambda_C confirms that deleting the assigned size-one value alone does not repair the printed completion.

Orientation reversal or any common nonzero parameter scaling preserves nonzero residual. Rank-dependent changes or poles in x change the question. For example, over Q((x)) all distinct nodes have unit differences and finite Chinese remainder interpolation permits arbitrary values; this does not identify that localized limit with a localization of the original limit. Casson zero makes this obstruction vanish and proves no existence. The constant1 family is a positive control.

Supporting reports were checked on their own mechanisms. The higher-jet statement follows by projecting to coefficient leveld+1 and comparing a fixed rank-coordinate representative with lifts: the discrepancy is a product ofd+1 node differences and vanishes modulo x^{d+1}. The coefficient of x^d in q^{nj} is binomial(nj,d), giving rational degree≤d, integer-valued in n. The modulo-prime bridge uses Phi_p(1+x)=p+binomial(p,2)x=0 in F_p[x]/x² for oddp, and rational uniqueness over infinitely many large primes. This corroborates the directly cited Taylor theorem. The trace-form Casimir identity sum_ij[E_ij,[E_ji,X]]=2nX−2Tr(X)I gives theta2n(n²−1). A raw Killing metricK=2nB changes degree-d graph weight by(2n)^−d, requiring the corresponding parameter conversion; KLO's actual Killing metric and quantum-dimension/framing formulas were inspected. No unconverted raw Killing weight is used as the main proof.

## New boundary falsification: complete torsion criterion

Let C be any commutative ring and lambda in C, and let f(n)=lambda(n³−n). This slope sequence is affine on all positive integers if and only if6lambda=0. Necessity: its second differences at successive triples1,2,3 and2,3,4 are12lambda and18lambda; their difference is6lambda. Sufficiency: every integer n³−n is divisible by6, so all f(n) vanish when6lambda=0. This proof works in every C and requires no cancellation. It makes the torsion exception exact: the first triple alone can miss the obstruction modulo4, where12=0 but18=2; modulo6 all cubic slopes vanish. Over Z the required6lambda=0 forces lambda=0, consistent with the theorem. The new independent_torsion_probe.py checks7259 coefficient/modulus pairs and100 cases where the first triple alone is misleading, under actual optimization0/1/2. The proof above, not those finite controls, establishes the general statement.

The all-tail derivation, the finite-coordinate proof, and the established topology inputs have distinct evidentiary roles. No finite PASS is promoted to a universal topology, priority, formal-proof, source-reading or sandbox claim.
''')
